English "must" is sometimes to encode,  in contrast to "have to", that the
speaker is the source of the obligation. So "e'i mi cliva" would be like "I
must go", while "ei mi cliva" would be like "I should go" or "I have to
go". But these meanings are modal rather than illocutionary.

--And.
